              "minAge": 6,
              "maxAge": 99
            }
          ],
          "coolFacts": [
            {
              "text": "The Thar Desert is one of the most POPULATED deserts in the world! Millions of people live across the Thar region! <�",
              "minAge": 6,
              "maxAge": 99
            },
            {
              "text": "Some sand dunes are 150 meters tall - that's like a 50-story building made of sand! <�",
              "minAge": 6,
              "maxAge": 99
            },
            {
              "text": "The temperature difference between day and night is CRAZY - 50�C during day, winter nights can become very cold! Your body wouldn't know what to do! <!",
              "minAge": 3,
              "maxAge": 99
            },
            {
              "text": "The night sky has Dark desert skies can offer excellent opportunities for stargazing and the Milky Way galaxy across the sky! <",
              "minAge": 3,
              "maxAge": 99
            },
            {
              "text": "Jaisalmer Fort is a GOLDEN FORT literally IN the middle of the desert - it glows at sunset! <�",
              "minAge": 3,
              "maxAge": 99
            },
            {
              "text": "The The Pushkar Fair is held annually in Rajasthan, traditionally around the Kartik Purnima period. <�",
              "minAge": 8,
              "maxAge": 99
            },
            {
              "text": "Thar used to be GREEN and have lots of water 4000 years ago - then climate changed! <
",
              "minAge": 8,
              "maxAge": 99
            },
            {
              "text": "The desert is slowly EXPANDING due to climate change - it's growing bigger every year! <",
              "minAge": 3,
              "maxAge": 99
            }
          ],
          "didYouKnow": {
            "text": "The Thar Desert is home to one of the rarest cats in the world - the Indian Desert Cat! It's smaller than a house cat and hunts at night! =1",
            "minAge": 3,
            "maxAge": 99
          },
          "tryThis": {
            "text": "Visit the Thar Desert at night and lie on the sand looking up! You'll see the Milky Way galaxy stretching across the entire sky - it's so amazing that you'll forget to breathe! (",
            "minAge": 3,
            "maxAge": 99
          },
          "narration": "The Thar Desert is AMAZING! <�\n\nIt's a heavily inhabited desert region! Millions of people live across the Thar region! How? They know incredible desert secrets passed down through their families for thousands of years!\n\nThe size is HUGE - 200,000 km�! That's BIGGER than the entire UK! Imagine that!\n\nThe sand dunes are SO TALL - some are 150 meters high! That's like looking up at a 40-story building, but made of SAND! <�\n\nThe temperature swings are CRAZY! In summer it's 50�C - hotter than your home oven! But at night it drops to -5�C and it's freezing! Your body wouldn't know what to do!\n\nBut here's the COOLEST part: At night, there are NO city lights! So you can see the ENTIRE Milky Way galaxy across the sky! It looks like someone poured milk across the sky! ( Over 1000 stars are visible!\n\nThe Thar Desert is home to SO many cool animals:\n- Camels =*\n- Lions (wild ones!) >�\n- Desert foxes >�\n- Gazelles >�\n- Eagles >�\n- Snakes (stay away!) =\n- Desert lizards >�\n\nAnd plants too! Date palms (you can eat the dates!), acacia trees, and tough desert shrubs! <4\n\nLong, long ago - 4,000 years ago - this area was GREEN and had lots of water! But then the climate changed and it became a desert. Now it's slowly expanding because of climate change.\n\nWhen you visit the Thar, you can:\n- Ride camels across the sand! =*\n- Sleep in desert camps under the stars! �\n- Watch sunsets that paint the sky orange, red, and purple! <\n- Watch sunrise when the sand turns golden! <\n- Explore Jaisalmer Fort - a golden fort in the middle of the desert! <�\n- Visit Pushkar for the camel fair and hot springs! =%\n\nBest time to visit? October to March! Summer is way too hot - stay away in June-August! <\n\nThe Thar Desert teaches us that even in harsh, extreme places, life finds a way! 5 million people, thousands of animals, and amazing plants have all adapted to survive! That's the power of nature! <"
        },
