            },
            {
              "text": "Chokha: mashed, roasted eggplant, potato, and tomato! <F",
              "minAge": 3,
              "maxAge": 99
            },
            {
              "text": "Served with a drizzle of pure ghee (clarified butter)! >�",
              "minAge": 3,
              "maxAge": 99
            },
            {
              "text": "A filling, protein-rich, energy-packed meal! =�",
              "minAge": 3,
              "maxAge": 99
            },
            {
              "text": "Sattu (roasted gram flour) is a Bihar specialty ingredient! <>",
              "minAge": 3,
              "maxAge": 99
            },
            {
              "text": "Thekua: a sweet fried wheat snack, big during festivals! <j",
              "minAge": 3,
              "maxAge": 99
            },
            {
              "text": "Simple, rustic ingredients from Bihar's farms! =�",
              "minAge": 3,
              "maxAge": 99
            },
            {
              "text": "A beloved street food and home-cooked classic! <}",
              "minAge": 3,
              "maxAge": 99
            },
            {
              "text": "Eaten across the state, from villages to cities! <�",
              "minAge": 3,
              "maxAge": 99
            }
          ],
          "coolFacts": [
            {
              "text": "Litti is traditionally roasted directly over hot coals or cow-dung fires for its smoky flavor! =%",
              "minAge": 3,
              "maxAge": 99
            },
            {
              "text": "Sattu, the stuffing, is a nutritious roasted-gram flour used in many Bihari dishes! <>",
              "minAge": 3,
              "maxAge": 99
            },
            {
              "text": "Litti Chokha is often called Bihar's answer to the baked potato - hearty and simple! >T",
              "minAge": 3,
              "maxAge": 99
            },
            {
              "text": "Thekua cookies are a must-have during the Chhath Puja festival! <j",
              "minAge": 3,
              "maxAge": 99
            },
            {
              "text": "The dish became popular across India as migrant Bihari workers carried the recipe with them! =�",
              "minAge": 3,
              "maxAge": 99
            }
          ],
          "didYouKnow": {
            "text": "Litti is traditionally cooked over an open fire made from dried cow-dung cakes, which gives it a distinct smoky flavor that's hard to recreate in a regular oven! =%",
            "minAge": 3,
            "maxAge": 99
          },
          "tryThis": {
            "text": "Ask a grown-up to help you roast something (like marshmallows or bread) over an open flame, and notice how the smoke changes the flavor! =%",
            "minAge": 3,
            "maxAge": 99
          },
          "narration": "Litti Chokha is Bihar's proudest comfort food - round balls of wheat dough stuffed with spiced sattu (roasted gram flour), traditionally roasted right over an open fire until smoky and golden. =%\n\nThey're served alongside Chokha, a smashed mix of roasted eggplant, potato, and tomato, with a drizzle of ghee on top for good measure.\n\nDuring festivals like Chhath Puja, families also make Thekua, a sweet fried wheat cookie that fills homes with a delicious aroma. <j"
