          "minAge": 3,
          "maxAge": 99
        },
        "narration": "Nagaland packs incredible diversity into one small mountain state - 16 major tribes, each with its own language, shawl pattern, and traditions. <�\n\nEvery December, they all come together for the Hornbill Festival, nicknamed the 'Festival of Festivals', filling the air with music, dance, and delicious smoky food. <�\n\nBeyond the celebrations, Nagaland carries deep history too - from the pivotal Battle of Kohima in World War II to the flower-filled Dz�kou Valley, often called the 'Valley of Flowers of the East'. <8"
      },
