        "en": {
          "title": "<4 KERALA - God's Own Country!",
          "emoji": "<4",
          "mainText": "With palm-lined backwaters, misty tea gardens, and India's highest literacy rate, it's easy to see why Kerala calls itself 'God's Own Country'!",
          "keyFacts": [
            {
              "text": "Nicknamed 'God's Own Country'! <4",
              "minAge": 3,
              "maxAge": 99
            },
            {
              "text": "Highest literacy rate in India (~96%)! =�",
              "minAge": 3,
              "maxAge": 99
            },
            {
              "text": "Famous backwaters stretch over 900 km! <
",
              "minAge": 6,
              "maxAge": 99
            },
            {
              "text": "Munnar: misty hills covered in tea gardens! <C",
              "minAge": 3,
              "maxAge": 99
            },
            {
              "text": "Ayurveda (ancient Indian medicine system) thrives here! <?",
              "minAge": 8,
              "maxAge": 99
            },
            {
              "text": "Kathakali: a dramatic classical dance-drama form! <�",
              "minAge": 3,
              "maxAge": 99
            },
            {
              "text": "Spice trade history - pepper was once called 'black gold'! <6",
              "minAge": 6,
              "maxAge": 99
            },
            {
              "text": "Onam: Kerala's biggest harvest festival, with boat races and flower art! <�",
              "minAge": 3,
              "maxAge": 99
            },
            {
              "text": "First Indian state with a democratically elected communist government (1957)! <�",
              "minAge": 3,
              "maxAge": 99
            },
            {
              "text": "Home to the world-famous Periyar Wildlife Sanctuary! =",
              "minAge": 6,
              "maxAge": 99
            }
          ],
          "coolFacts": [
            {
              "text": "Kerala's spice trade with ancient Rome, Arabia, and China dates back over 2,000 years! <6",
              "minAge": 8,
              "maxAge": 99
            },
            {
              "text": "Kathakali performers spend hours applying elaborate makeup before every dramatic performance! <�",
              "minAge": 3,
              "maxAge": 99
            },
            {
              "text": "Kerala was the first place in India (and among the first in the world) to elect a communist government through voting! <�",
              "minAge": 3,
              "maxAge": 99
            },
            {
              "text": "Munnar's tea gardens roll across misty hills as far as the eye can see! <C",
              "minAge": 3,
              "maxAge": 99
            },
            {
              "text": "Ayurveda treatments and wellness retreats draw visitors to Kerala from all over the world! <?",
              "minAge": 3,
              "maxAge": 99
            }
          ],
          "didYouKnow": {
            "text": "Kerala's spice trade, especially in black pepper, was so valuable that ancient traders called it 'black gold' - pepper from Kerala's hills once traveled all the way to Rome and beyond, over 2,000 years ago! <6",
            "minAge": 8,
            "maxAge": 99
          },
          "tryThis": {
            "text": "Look at a jar of black pepper at home and imagine it being so valuable that ships sailed across oceans just to trade for it! <6",
            "minAge": 3,
            "maxAge": 99
          },
          "narration": "Kerala calls itself 'God's Own Country' - and between its palm-lined backwaters, misty tea gardens, and lush spice forests, it's easy to see why. <4\n\nOver 2,000 years ago, traders sailed from as far as Rome just to buy Kerala's black pepper, once so valuable it was nicknamed 'black gold'. <6\n\nToday, Kerala boasts India's highest literacy rate, a thriving classical dance tradition in colorful Kathakali performances, and the joyful Onam harvest festival, celebrated with flower carpets and thrilling boat races. <�"
        },
