          "narration": "The Andaman and Nicobar Islands are unlike anywhere else in India - a scattered chain of over 500 islands, with India's only active volcano quietly smoking on Barren Island. <\n\nDeep in this island world lives the Sentinelese tribe, believed to be one of the most isolated peoples on Earth - so protected that outside contact is against the law, to keep them safe. =�\n\nAbove the waves, powder-white beaches and vibrant coral reefs draw travelers from around the world, while below the surface, gentle dugongs graze quietly on the sea floor. = "
