          "narration": "Chandigarh has an unusual job - being the capital of not one, but two different states, Punjab and Haryana. And its language reflects that beautifully! <\n\nPunjabi, written in its own Gurmukhi script, mixes easily with Hindi and English on the city's streets, in its schools, and in its lively Bhangra music scene. <�\n\nIt's a genuinely trilingual capital, where greeting someone with 'Sat Sri Akal' feels just as natural as saying 'Namaste' or 'Hello'. =O"
