          "narration": "For almost 18 years, a government worker named Nek Chand had a secret. At night, after his regular job ended, he quietly built an entire fantasy garden out of things other people threw away - broken tiles, old bangles, and industrial scraps. <\n\nWhen officials finally discovered his secret creation in 1975, they were so amazed they decided to protect and expand it, instead of tearing it down.\n\nToday, the Rock Garden spreads across 40 acres, filled with hundreds of sculptures, waterfalls, and winding paths - proof that incredible art can be made from things others simply discard. {"
