          "narration": "Chandigarh earned its nickname 'The City Beautiful' the hard way - through careful, deliberate planning, right down to its numbered sectors and peaceful, man-made Sukhna Lake. <3\n\nDesigned by the famous architect Le Corbusier after India's independence, it remains one of the best examples anywhere in the world of a city built entirely from a single, thoughtful plan. <�\n\nToday, as the shared capital of Punjab and Haryana, and home to the artistic wonder of the Rock Garden, Chandigarh proves that a city can be organized, green, and full of creativity, all at once. <�"
